        "title": "Symbiosis: Zooxanthellae, Photosynthesis, and the Bleaching Trigger",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The coral-zooxanthellae partnership is one of the most consequential symbioses on Earth. It is a nutritional mutualism: the photosynthetic algae supply up to 90% of the coral's energy, and the coral provides a protected cell interior with CO₂ and dissolved inorganic nitrogen. The relationship is also catastrophically fragile — a few degrees of excess heat for a few weeks triggers its breakdown, which is the mechanism behind coral bleaching."
    }
